WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:01.179
---

00:00:01.179 --> 00:00:06.831
Miquella is many things. A fundamentalist.
The Unalloyed. Creator of the Haligtree, Lord

00:00:06.831 --> 00:00:15.330
of the Eclipse, Saint Trina of the Cradlesong,
and a fearsome empyrean who has been captured,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.130
but is unresponsive - for now.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:23.430
And..after watching this video, I think you'll
agree that Miquella is a topic that almost

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:29.061
HAS to be explored further in some upcoming
DLC. For how could they not be? Their character

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.620
is surely too major, too foreshadowed, and
too intriguing, to just ignore.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.620
So..let's learn everything, that there is
to know.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.620
---

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.620
Miquella is many things. The Unalloyed. St
Trina. Twin brother to Malenia, and not just

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.620
a Demigod, but an Empyrean, who is said to
possess the very allure of a god.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.620
And..after watching this video, I think you'll
agree that Miquella is a topic that almost

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.620
HAS to be explored further in some upcoming
DLC. For how could they not be? Their character

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.620
is too major, too foreshadowed, and too intriguing,
to just ignore.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.620
Of course, knowing From Software, we'll probably
get DLC about the spirit jellyfish / boc / or

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.620
something instead..I don't know. So I guess
we'll just have to wait and see.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.620
---

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.620
But until then, let's learn all there is to
know about Miquella.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.559
For starters, Miquella is the demigod child
of Queen Marika, and King Consort Radagon..who,

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:51.640
as I'm sure you're well aware - are the same
being. You can learn more about the timeline

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.239
of events from my other videos, but basically
- after Radagon left Rennala - the Academy

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:04.930
told Radagon to go fuck himself, and Radagon
took that literally - siring a third set of

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:10.250
demigod children all on his own, who were
the twins Miquella, and Malenia

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.520
Which brings us to an extremely important
description - the Remembrance of the Rot Goddess,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.049
which tells us that the twins "Miquella and
Malenia are both the children of a single

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:16.049
god. As such, they are both Empyreans, but
suffered afflictions from birth. Miquella

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:17.049
was cursed with eternal childhood, and Malenia
harbored rot within."

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:21.250
The Nascent Butterfly item appears to represent
Miquella, and it elaborates on his state of

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:26.930
eternal childhood, stating that it "appears
as if it's just emerged from its cocoon for

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:33.010
its entire life". Indeed, the word "Nascent"
means that something is "Just coming into

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:39.990
existence, and beginning to display signs
of future potential".

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:46.060
And I think this "eternally nascent" characteristic
is incredibly important to Miquella's character.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:52.900
For Miquella and Malenia both seem to occupy
opposite sides of the life and death cycle.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:58.510
That's not to say that Miquella represents
life and Malenia represents death, rather,

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:04.409
it seems like both land somewhere in the middle
of each process. Malenia is constantly resisting

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:09.890
her scarlet rot out of sheer will, and is
in this perpetual state of dying, and Miquella

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:15.870
is in this constant state of nascence - newly
born, and showing an abundance of life and

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.690
burgeoning potential. Special thanks to Quelaag,
for pointing this out to me.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:28.050
And that word, "Abundance", is actually an
extremely key word for Miquella. For example,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:34.020
there's this cut weapon, called the "Abundance
and Decay Twinblade", which symbolises the

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:39.930
twins, and suggests that the twins were "born
from an inseparable fate", and hold the "Runes

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.420
of both Abundance and Decay" between them.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:51.550
Also, the word "abundance' shows up a lot
in the cut dialogue of a character, who I

00:02:51.550 --> 00:03:05.480
think it's fair to assume, is Miquella. Here,
he talks about his ability to make life flourish,

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.480
stating:

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.800
"This is for thee.
Mine abundance, my drop of dew.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.390
Quench thy thirst, throughout thy frame.
Blossom and burgeon, time and again.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.489
Grow larger, stronger.
Until the day cometh.

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:23.780
When thou canst share in my dream.
Elden Ring, O Elden Ring.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.140
Beget Order most elegant, from my tender reverie."

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:33.760
So again: the abundance of Miquella IS cut
content, and you shouldn't really take it

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:39.989
as canon - but it does give us a deeper look
- not only at the powers Miquella might have

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:43.970
had, but also that the world he could create.
This character goes on to say:

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:48.420
"If thou covetest the throne,
Impress my vision upon thine heart.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.060
In the new world of thy making,
all things will flourish,

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.189
whether graceful, or malign."

00:03:54.189 --> 00:04:01.129
I love that final line. "All things will flourish,
whether graceful, or malign". Miquella isn't

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:08.180
enforcing any notions of good or evil here
- and in the new world of his making, he simply

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.500
wants all things to flourish.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:19.030
And 
Miquella certainly is one of the few beings

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:25.360
capable of creating this "new world". That's
because he is an "Empyrean", one of the very

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.870
few who were candidates, chosen by the Two
Fingers, to succeed Queen Marika and become

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.260
a god, to usher in a new age

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:40.169
Now, we could go into an entire debate about
WHY the twins are valid Empyreans and WHY

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:45.120
they were born afflicted..but honestly, that
could be a video of its own - so for now,

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.770
I'll give the simple answer. [Source: Remembrance
of the Rot Goddess]. That is, that they were

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:55.270
probably valid Empyreans because they have
singular parentage from a god - but that this

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:00.690
singular parentage was probably also responsible
for their afflictions as well..due to the

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.500
almost..incestual implications of such a thing.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:09.010
Why do I feel like George R R Martin wrote
this part..?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:13.120
---
Miquella, the Fundamentalist

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.940
Anyway, let's move into the early childhood
years of..Miquella's...eternal..childhood.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:24.160
Miquella's early years were clearly quite
inspired by their father, Radagon, who fostered

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:30.479
a bit of a fundamentalist streak in his prodigal
son. Miquella would even go on to invent fundamentalist

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:35.980
incantations of his own, dubbed "Discus of
Light" and "Triple Rings of Light", which

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.850
he gifted to his father.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:47.420
These gifts reveal that Radagon and Miquella
had a good relationship, and they represent

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:54.430
those two key fundamentals of the Golden Order
- that there is a law of causality - a branching

00:05:54.430 --> 00:06:00.770
cause and effect , but also that there is
a law of regression - that all things yearn

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.850
eternally to converge [Source: Law of Regression]
(show the discus's on screen).

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.680
In gratitude, Radagon countered with a gift
of his own - Radagon's Rings of Light. A singular

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.680
ring, , perhaps showcasing that Radagon was
all about regression, and being whole

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.479
These incantations would go on to become become
core fundamentalist spells, as they are true

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:19.510
to those two concepts that form the basis
of Golden Order fundamentalism

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:25.380
But there is another aspect of Golden Order
fundamentalism, and that is the persecution

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:30.980
of Those Who Live In Death. Hunters of these
undead would attempt to stamp them out with

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:36.610
spells such as Order's Blade and Litany of
Proper Death, which deal additional damage

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.860
against TWLID, and prevent them from resurrecting.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:45.560
Put simply, Those Who Live In Death exist
because of Godwyn the Golden, one of the early

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:52.310
sons of Marika and Godfrey, who was killed
with a fragment of the Rune of Death, which

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.629
now spreads its undeath throughout the lands
between, via deathroot

00:06:56.629 --> 00:07:02.669
And...there's an entire debate that we could
have here, about whether the persecution of

00:07:02.669 --> 00:07:08.350
Those Who Live In Death is even true to the
core principles of fundamentalism. Goldmask

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:14.660
certainly doesn't seem to think so. In fact,
according to the "Order Healing" spell, Goldmask

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:20.470
lamented the hunters of Those Who Live In
Death, deeming them fanatics, who wanted nothing

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.460
more than an absolute evil to contend with.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:29.550
And the reason I bring up this debate is because...you
could argue that Miquella was on the side

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:36.569
of these fanatics, as he created multiple
weapons that were capable of effectively slaying

00:07:36.569 --> 00:07:37.879
Those Who Live in Death.

00:07:37.879 --> 00:07:45.490
For example, this is Golden Epitaph, "a sword
made to commemorate the death of Godwyn the

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.430
Golden, first of the demigods to die". It
is "Infused with the humble prayer of a young

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:57.819
boy", and reads "O brother, lord brother,
please die a true death."

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:05.960
Clearly, the young boy in question here..is
Miquella. We can infer this, because the sigil

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:12.819
that appears when you use this Blade's skill
is the Haligtree sigil. And once activated,

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:18.750
this ability, called "last rites", imbues
the sword with a holy power that prevents

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.970
Those Who Live In Death from reviving.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:28.430
What's really interesting here though, is
that this weapon points towards an early kinship

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:34.849
between Miquella, and Godwyn. A relationship,
which might have made it all the more painful

00:08:34.849 --> 00:08:41.570
when Godwyn's soul perished but his body remained,
spawning deathroot. This is interesting, as

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:48.269
it gives Miquella a legitimate emotional grievance
against Those Who Live In Death. This is almost

00:08:48.269 --> 00:08:57.570
ironic, considering we previously established
Miquella as this character who wants all life

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:07.220
to flourish - but I guess that principle might
not extend to Those Who Live In Death, hey?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:14.250
Miquella's relationship with Godwyn is potentially
strengthened when we consider this statue,

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:21.230
found in Elphael, before the Haligtree. It
depicts a larger figure, who is clearly embracing

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:27.300
the two empyrean twins, Miquella, and Malenia..but
then..who is this larger figure?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:32.930
It could be their parent, Marika or Radagon
- but then..it doesn't have their signature

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:39.959
hair braid, and instead has long, wavy hair.
What's more, the statue asset is flat-chested,

00:09:39.959 --> 00:09:45.830
which rules out Marika, at least. So, after
reading a good amount of debate online about

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:51.839
this, I think it's a fair conclusion to say
that this statue represents Godwyn - who himself

00:09:51.839 --> 00:09:54.480
does seem to have long, wavy hair.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:03.230
This statue being enshrined here really tells
a story. A story of two afflicted siblings

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:11.810
supported by their older brother, who was
the first Demigod to die. But it's not the

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.209
only statue in this location.

00:10:14.209 --> 00:10:20.209
Far more prominent in the area, are these
statues; of two siblings left alone, after

00:10:20.209 --> 00:10:26.170
their brother died - with one who was forced
to remain as a young child, and another who

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:33.140
grew - losing limbs to rot, and decay.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:37.440
These statues are everywhere in the Haligtree,
and tell the sorrowful story of these two

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:44.260
siblings. They are an early sign of Miquella's
extreme empathy for his sister, and his desperate

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:48.860
attempts to give her relief from her terrifying
condition.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:54.870
And so, "the young Miquella abandoned fundamentalism,
for it could do nothing to treat Malenia's

00:10:54.870 --> 00:11:07.660
accursed rot. This was the beginning..of unalloyed
gold".

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:08.660
---

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:14.130
So what is unalloyed gold? Well, an alloy
is created when you combine metals - usually

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:20.529
because you want to create a stronger compound,
at the expense of its purity. So if we were

00:11:20.529 --> 00:11:34.580
to view Marika's Golden Order as if it were
a metal, then it would definitely be an alloyed

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:40.600
metal. Just think of all the foreign powers
that it's absorbed in the interest of strength:

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:46.149
For example, Godfrey and his crucible knights
were enlisted to devastate Marika's enemies..

00:11:46.149 --> 00:11:51.769
the ancient dragons were won over and became
a part of Leyndell's forces [Source: Gravel

00:11:51.769 --> 00:11:54.320
Stone Seal, Malformed Dragon Set, Lightning
Spear]...even the house of the Erdtree and

00:11:54.320 --> 00:12:02.510
the Moon were married. LiterallyAfter all,
as Miriel puts it, "all things can be conjoined"

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:07.959
under the Golden Order..so I think Marika
was definitely open to fusing factions and

00:12:07.959 --> 00:12:14.850
ideologies - as long as it made her treasured
Golden Order alloy, stronger.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:20.680
So hopefully now, you understand what I mean
when I say that Miquella's gold is unalloyed.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:27.890
It is pure. It is untainted. It is, perhaps,
a singular ideology. And if you subscribe

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:33.040
to the idea that the cut content is still
representative of Miquella, then I would say

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:39.510
that his ideology is what I had Miquella quote
earlier - that in his new world, all things

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:50.220
should be allowed to flourish, whether graceful
or malign - though that is of course, cut

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.130
content, and my own speculation.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:58.350
But Miquella's unalloyed gold couldn't have
just been this metaphysical concept of pure

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:05.560
ideology - it was a physical material as well.
For example, this is an unalloyed gold water

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:12.250
lily, said to be beloved by Miquella ]. This
is a bewitching branch, blessed with an incantation

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:18.260
of unalloyed gold Unalloyed gold decorated
the armour and shields of his soldiers, it

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:23.820
was inserted into their weapons - and most
importantly, perhaps, it was forged into a

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.949
set of armour for his sister, Malenia

00:13:26.949 --> 00:13:33.760
Because remember - the whole reason Miquella
embraced unalloyed gold, was because he thought

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:39.880
that it could treat his sister's accursed
rot, while fundamentalism could not. And he

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.240
was right.

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:48.029
For Malenia's scarlet rot is no mere disease.
It's literally the divine essence of an outer

00:13:48.029 --> 00:13:54.290
god , and Malenia is its vessel , that will
one day bloom into a true goddess

00:13:54.290 --> 00:14:00.019
But unalloyed gold is one of the few materials
in the game, that can ward away such meddling

00:14:00.019 --> 00:14:12.690
of the outer 
gods . Personally, I think that speaks to

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:20.760
the purity of Miquella's unalloyed gold ideology
- but if that's not enough reason for you,

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:26.520
then Quelaag has a great video where she breaks
things down at a chemical level

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:34.329
At any rate, Miquella crafted needles of unalloyed
gold, which could be inserted into the tortured

00:14:34.329 --> 00:14:41.709
flesh of one afflicted by rot to alleviate
their suffering, and forestall its effects

00:14:41.709 --> 00:14:46.660
And true to the needle's description, the
outer god of rot isn't the only one affected

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:53.110
by this - our character actually uses the
final version of this needle to subdue the

00:14:53.110 --> 00:15:00.930
outer god of frenzy, if you decide not to
be a terrible person, and burn down the world

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:06.139
When we first find Miquella's Needle - it's
been broken. Snapped in half, and picked up

00:15:06.139 --> 00:15:10.029
by a commander at the very center of the scarlet
swamp.

00:15:10.029 --> 00:15:15.270
But once repaired, we can give the golden
needle to Millicent, proving that it does

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:21.589
indeed work to forestall the rotting sickness,
to remove pain, and nightmares from the afflicted.

00:15:21.589 --> 00:15:24.870
It is, after all, lovingly crafted by Miquella
himself.

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.430
Now, let me have a look at the needle.
Hmm.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:31.890
Well, well, this is a marvel indeed.
The work of a true artisan…a meticulous,

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:36.070
bold craftsman who grasps the essence of life.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:41.420
In crafting these needles, and pursuing unalloyed
gold, Miquella is attempting to save his sister

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:46.800
from her affliction. It seems like an objectively
good deed - which is a rare sight, in Elden

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:58.220
Ring. Especially for a demigod, whose strengths
have been known to tip them towards madness

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:04.170
So it's no wonder that Malenia venerated her
brother. She is a character of undefeated

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:10.790
prowess , an empyrean, no less - and yet she
dedicated her blade to Miquella, and Miquella

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:16.190
alone. For she believes that "He possesses
the wisdom, the allure, of a god" and that

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.459
"he is the most fearsome Empyrean of all"

00:16:19.459 --> 00:16:24.720
The story of their bond and duty to one another
is legendary - something that becomes quite

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:30.230
clear when we explore Miquella's Haligtree,
and see these statues depicting their embrace,

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:35.160
all around. If you were one of the many defiled
outcasts in Elden Ring, you too might have

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:41.580
felt inspired by this story..and might have
felt inclined to earn Miquella's favor and

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:45.850
make the long pilgrimage towards salvation.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:51.130
Towards the distant, divine Haligtree, and
its brace, that was Miquella's domain.

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:54.930
---
Miquella of the Haligtree

00:16:54.930 --> 00:17:00.889
So first, what even is the Haligtree? Well,
there is good evidence that it's a sort of

00:17:00.889 --> 00:17:07.329
Erdtree. For one, Erdtree Avatars have clearly
emerged from it, which they only do in order

00:17:07.329 --> 00:17:12.990
to protect the Erdtree's own offspring . And
then there's the Haligtree Knight Armor, which

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:18.360
confirms that "the Haligtree ultimately failed
to grow into an Erdtree"

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:28.210
And this made me wonder..when exactly was
the Haligtree planted, then? Was it planted

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.400
before, or after the shattering of the Elden
Ring?

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:36.570
Because when the Elden Ring was shattered,
Golden Seeds "flew from the Erdtree, scattering

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:42.840
across the various lands, as if life itself
knew that its end had come". These seeds create

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:48.710
these little illusory trees, and likely spawned
the Minor Erdtrees, so I feel like it's a

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:54.580
fair assumption that Miquella might have planted
the Haligtree from an Erdtree Seed. And if

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:59.160
that was indeed the case, then it should have
happened after the shattering - for before

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:04.220
that, the Erdtree was considered "perfect
and eternal", and it wasn't even believed

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.409
that Erdtree seeds could exist

00:18:06.409 --> 00:18:12.230
On the flip side, the Golden Epitaph sword
we mentioned earlier likely existed before

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:17.679
the Shattering, as it was created to commemorate
Godwyn's death. And this sword displays the

00:18:17.679 --> 00:18:24.500
haligtree sigil when its weapon art is activated,
so..one could infer that the Haligtree must

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:29.220
have existed at this point too. So I guess
it's always possible that Miquella somehow

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:35.809
procured an Erdtree Seed before the shattering,
or simply grew it from his own being, as a

00:18:35.809 --> 00:18:39.350
scion of the Golden Bough

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:44.940
Whatever the case, Miquella clearly decided
that growing such a tree was important, and

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:51.429
even went so far as to water it with his own
blood This confirms..that the Erdtree is indeed

00:18:51.429 --> 00:18:56.220
a blood sucking parasite. Just kidding. Kind
of. You have to admit though, It is pretty

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:00.210
disturbing that an Erdtree could flourish
in such a manner.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:05.100
But this does lead us to the final question
which is - why was the Haligtree planted?

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:06.809
What is the point of it?

00:19:06.809 --> 00:19:11.039
And at the end of the, the main reason is
always going to be because it is like the

00:19:11.039 --> 00:19:19.470
Erdtree. I did just spend a few minutes comparing
them, after all. The Erdtree is this enormous

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:26.380
icon of power and faith in the Lands Between,
so evoking that and inspiring worship is clearly

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:29.720
a valuable thing
But the Erdtree was only really of an icon

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:35.090
of faith in its later years . Before that,
it was a symbol of abundance, with light as

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:41.010
warm as the gentle sun, gradually healing
all those who bathed in its rays . But perhaps

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:48.850
most importantly, it would drip sacred dew.
Sap, or tears, that could bestow blessings

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:57.880
, form crystal tears, and even be embedded
into talismans . Naturally, this was an extremely

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:05.809
value symbol for Miquella to evoke, since
he is himself associated with dew, and abundance.

00:20:05.809 --> 00:20:12.059
And his Haligtree did drip with dew. The greenish
amber of the Haligtree can even be seen in

00:20:12.059 --> 00:20:18.580
cut content items, which I speculate is mingled
with a bit of Miquella's own blood. That signature

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:26.020
green hue of haligtree amber is also seen
in the Haligtree Knight's Sword, which was

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:32.370
modeled after the Carian Knights' own swords,
except it was embedded with amber instead

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:41.390
of glintstone

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:46.419
But what else does the Haligtree add in terms
of value? Well, the Haligtree itself is something

00:20:46.419 --> 00:20:52.870
of a vessel, fit for a god. Miquella plants
himself inside it. Malenia returns home to

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:57.100
it. And speaking of it being a home, many
other creatures have made their home within

00:20:57.100 --> 00:21:00.020
the tree..and within the brace that supports
it.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:05.190
And I guess you could argue that the Haligtree
might also be a sort of tool, to be used.

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:10.620
After all, Marika puts the Erdtree to use
in such a way, using its roots to absorb people

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:16.929
after their death, and perhaps even its branches
to rebirth life. And then the Erdtree is later

00:21:16.929 --> 00:21:23.300
used as a prison, with thorns that are almost
entirely impenetrable. But I don't think Miquella

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.080
planned to use the Haligtree in such a way.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:30.510
Perhaps the biggest difference between the
Haligtree and the Erdtree, is that the Haligtree

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:37.170
was built in a largely inhospitable region.
It is extremely difficult to reach, and unlike

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:42.179
the Erdtree, it might not really be designed
for the benefit of the vast majority of the

00:21:42.179 --> 00:21:47.529
world. As it stands, the Haligtree strikes
me as being more like the Painted World from

00:21:47.529 --> 00:21:53.370
Dark Souls - a place for the outcasts, the
heretical, and the malign. Not to mention

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:57.690
the low, and the meek, who are specifically
named out in the description of the Sacred

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.990
Crown Helm [Source: Sacred Crown Helm].

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:03.830
While many of the scarlet-rot afflicted seem
to be here because of the eventual decay of

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:10.370
the Haligtree, I think there are a number
of refugees already here - namely,

00:22:10.370 --> 00:22:17.710
the misbegotten ... the crystalian ... these
astray mages of Raya Lucaria, and of course,

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:23.000
Loretta, who deemed this place to be a great
haven for the despised albinaurics

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:28.890
The second generation albinaurics even carry
a weapon called the "Ivory Sickle", which

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:33.870
reads "These weapons are evidence of their
dedication to the Haligtree, despite never

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:39.659
having entered its presence." And yet, we
don't find a single albinauric within the

00:22:39.659 --> 00:22:46.779
Haligtree [NOTE: Unless you count Loretta].
Maybe they have yet to make the trip.

00:22:46.779 --> 00:22:55.419
It makes sense that the first generation of
albinaurics not to be here, though. Even Albus

00:22:55.419 --> 00:23:01.679
cites their faded legs as the reason for that
. And yet, we find them defending Miquella

00:23:01.679 --> 00:23:08.470
and his Haligtree all the same - at the Ordina
Liturgical Town, which takes us to the Haligtree

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:15.420
via a puzzle within an Evergaol. The word
"Liturgical" means "relating to public worship",

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:22.240
and the town is fittingly filled with many
statues of Miquella alone - cradling what

00:23:22.240 --> 00:23:26.429
might have become the Haligtree, but back
when it was a sapling.

00:23:26.429 --> 00:23:32.450
I also find it interesting that the Haligtree
is never called out as competing with the

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:39.220
Erdtree, or for housing these undesirables.
Perhaps the House of the Erdtree was happy

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:48.240
to see ungraceful folk leave, perhaps the
Haligtree was extremely well-hidden from everyone,

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:54.230
or perhaps Miquella could simply get away
with it, because he was beloved by all.

00:23:54.230 --> 00:23:59.010
The Bewitching Branch is an item that you
can create from Miquella's Lillies, and is

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:04.070
"blessed with an incantation of unalloyed
gold", and reads "The Empyrean Miquella is

00:24:04.070 --> 00:24:09.679
loved by many people. Indeed, he has learned
very well how to compel such affection.".

00:24:09.679 --> 00:24:14.871
And that second part, that says he has learned
well how to compel affection - to me, that's

00:24:14.871 --> 00:24:21.330
saying that Miquella is very good at knowing
how to inspire others' affection to his own

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:22.630
advantage.

00:24:22.630 --> 00:24:24.910
And nowhere is this more clear...than at Castle
Sol.

00:24:24.910 --> 00:24:32.980
---
Lord Miquella of the Eclipse

00:24:32.980 --> 00:24:37.941
This is the Haligtree Secret Medallion. It's
furnished with that signature green amber,

00:24:37.941 --> 00:24:44.010
and features the Haligtree in the background,
for it allows you to access a secret, lower

00:24:44.010 --> 00:24:49.120
level of the Grand Lift of Rold, and progress
through the consecrated snowfields to this

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:50.670
sacred place.

00:24:50.670 --> 00:24:56.190
Having both halves of this secret medallion
is therefore extremely desirable. For the

00:24:56.190 --> 00:24:58.480
medallion has another name, as "Miquella's
Favor".

00:24:58.480 --> 00:25:11.760
Miquella's favour can be yours…
Slaughter, slaughter, slaughter... The all-hearing

00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:29.730
slaughtered, but alas, it was for naught.
But all you need do, is snatch it from the

00:25:29.730 --> 00:25:31.099
big pot.

00:25:31.099 --> 00:25:36.650
Gideon is "the all-hearing" in this dialogue,
and slaughtered an entire village just for

00:25:36.650 --> 00:25:42.950
one half, but did not find it in Albus' possession.
But you can.

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:49.149
And the other half? It's at Castle Sol, right
before a nameless phantom..who says this:

00:25:49.149 --> 00:25:52.929
Lord Miquella, forgive me.
The sun has not been swallowed.

00:25:52.929 --> 00:25:55.990
Our prayers were lacking.
Your comrade remains soulless...

00:25:55.990 --> 00:26:00.130
I will never set my eyes upon it now...
Your divine Haligtree...

00:26:00.130 --> 00:26:08.529
So.. this phantom seemingly has one half of
the medallion, and yet he laments that he

00:26:08.529 --> 00:26:13.870
will now never set eyes upon the Haligtree.
To me, this suggests that Miquella might have

00:26:13.870 --> 00:26:19.350
been withholding the second half of the medallion
from him, or that this phantom believed that

00:26:19.350 --> 00:26:26.040
he could solicit the second half from Miquella
and make it to the Haligtree - if he achieved

00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:29.409
his goal here at Castle Sol.

00:26:29.409 --> 00:26:35.440
..but what exactly was supposed to happen
here at Castle Sol? What does it mean when

00:26:35.440 --> 00:26:41.150
the phantom says "the sun has not been swallowed.
Our prayers were lacking. Your comrade remains

00:26:41.150 --> 00:26:42.789
soulless"?

00:26:42.789 --> 00:26:48.909
It means that the residents of Castle Sol,
and Miquella, were attempting to restore the

00:26:48.909 --> 00:26:51.370
dead soul of Godwyn the Golden.

00:26:51.370 --> 00:26:56.220
And just to refresh your memory: when a fragment
of the rune of death was used to kill Godwyn,

00:26:56.220 --> 00:27:01.230
it was also being used at the exact same time,
to kill Ranni. So since they perished at the

00:27:01.230 --> 00:27:08.500
same time, Ranni lost her body, and Miquella's
demigod brother Godwyn perished in soul alone.

00:27:08.500 --> 00:27:15.470
And despite this death seeming so final, Miquella
clearly believes that some sort of ritual,

00:27:15.470 --> 00:27:19.710
performed here, could restore the soul of
his comrade.

00:27:19.710 --> 00:27:28.060
Ohh great sun! Frigid sun of Sol!
Surrender yourself to the eclipse!

00:27:28.060 --> 00:27:42.919
Grant life to the soulless bones!

00:27:42.919 --> 00:27:48.220
The question is...how?

00:27:48.220 --> 00:27:53.700
So at Castle Sol, we find the Eclipse shotel,
which reads "Storied sword and treasure of

00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:59.539
Castle Sol that depicts an eclipsed sun drained
of color. In Sol, the sight of an eclipse

00:27:59.539 --> 00:28:04.880
inspires a dreadful awe, preventing an onlooker
from averting his gaze". The most important

00:28:04.880 --> 00:28:09.020
part of this description though, is the part
that says it's the "storied sword" of Castle

00:28:09.020 --> 00:28:14.010
Sol, as this proves that the veneration of
the eclipse here, goes back a long way.

00:28:14.010 --> 00:28:19.570
But what does an eclipse represent? So according
to the Eclipse Crest shields, "The eclipsed

00:28:19.570 --> 00:28:42.120
sun, drained of color, is the protective star
of soulless demigods", and "the sun in eclipse

00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:47.179
is said to be the symbol of the Wandering
Mausoleum where the soulless demigods slumber".

00:28:47.179 --> 00:28:53.809
Note that it says "demigods", plural here.
This could be because the wandering mausoleums

00:28:53.809 --> 00:29:03.559
come to house many demigods from a gameplay
point of view, or it even be slightly lost

00:29:03.559 --> 00:29:08.770
in translation, as the Japanese version of
the description does not specify whether it's

00:29:08.770 --> 00:29:09.770
demigods, singular or plural. So I actually
think the slumbering demigod in question,

00:29:09.770 --> 00:29:11.380
is Godwyn - he is the only real candidate
for a comrade of Miquella who has lost his

00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:12.380
soul, after all. And as we established earlier,
Miquella had an affection for Godwyn, and

00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:13.380
lamented his inability to die a true death
[Source: Golden Epitaph]. So basically, I

00:29:13.380 --> 00:29:18.360
think the wandering mausoleums became necessary
when Godwyn died - as he was the first Demigod

00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:22.770
to die..so the mausoleums were intended to
be a resting place for him, but also for any

00:29:22.770 --> 00:29:30.080
future demigods, as their deaths suddenly
became possible, with the theft of Destined

00:29:30.080 --> 00:29:31.080
Death.

00:29:31.080 --> 00:29:36.580
The Mausoleum Knights themselves are these
headless soldiers who beheaded themselves,

00:29:36.580 --> 00:29:41.730
willingly following their master into death
. As such, they became these headless spirits,

00:29:41.730 --> 00:29:45.870
tied to the land so that they might defend
the walking mausoleums.

00:29:45.870 --> 00:29:51.211
They also carry eclipse-crested shields, and
the eclipse is said to "aid the mausoleum

00:29:51.211 --> 00:29:56.830
knights by keeping destined death at bay"
. It is their symbol, and by keeping destined

00:29:56.830 --> 00:30:01.860
death at bay, maybe it is helping to keep
their souls tied to the land?

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:06.980
We could speculate for a long time on how
the eclipse has this power. You could even

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:12.799
argue that this "protective star", is a sort
of outer god. It's simpler though, to just

00:30:12.799 --> 00:30:17.750
trust that Miquella knew what he was doing
with the eclipse at Castle Sol, where he wanted

00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:21.470
to block out the sun, and restore Godwyn's
soul.

00:30:21.470 --> 00:30:28.429
All that said, it's very important to remember:
that this ritual failed. According to this

00:30:28.429 --> 00:30:34.809
phantom, the "sun was not swallowed", and
so, the star of the eclipse did not listen

00:30:34.809 --> 00:30:36.990
to their prayers, and appear.

00:30:36.990 --> 00:30:42.279
But it's fascinating to learn that such a
thing might even be possible. That Godwyn,

00:30:42.279 --> 00:30:48.200
whose soul seems to be as dead as Ranni's
body..might actually not be?

00:30:48.200 --> 00:30:52.600
So if his soul is somewhere, where has it
fled to?

00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:57.840
A part of me wonders, if his soul is lost
somewhere...perhaps, within a dream.

00:30:57.840 --> 00:31:04.150
One theory I did come up with regarding the
eclipse, is that it might be able to bring

00:31:04.150 --> 00:31:11.559
Godwyn's soul back, by bringing about a sort
of artificial dusk. Those Who Live in Death

00:31:11.559 --> 00:31:18.010
are called the "duskborn", after all . There
is an association between night, and death,

00:31:18.010 --> 00:31:19.320
to be sure.

00:31:19.320 --> 00:31:24.620
And there is also an association between death,
and sleep. For example, when you pursue Fia's

00:31:24.620 --> 00:31:30.519
questline, you use her as a medium to enter
Godwyn's "deathbed dream", which is an entire

00:31:30.519 --> 00:31:37.100
dreamscape where the dragon Fortissax is futilely
fighting against the death in his companion.

00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:41.600
And then there's Rogier, who speaks this line
of dialogue, as he is on the precipice of

00:31:41.600 --> 00:31:43.780
succumbing to deathroot,

00:31:43.780 --> 00:31:49.860
Hmm. Maybe I should tell you.
Lately, I feel I'm on the precipice...

00:31:49.860 --> 00:31:53.289
Of falling into a deep...fathomless slumber.

00:31:53.289 --> 00:31:59.429
Later, Rogier does fight you, defending Fia
as one of her champions. So in conclusion:

00:31:59.429 --> 00:32:03.309
a realm of death does seem accessible through
dream.

00:32:03.309 --> 00:32:07.841
And this is the perfect time to mention..
that Miquella has an alter-ego. "Some say

00:32:07.841 --> 00:32:13.529
she is a comely young girl, others are sure
he is a boy" . This is where we must talk

00:32:13.529 --> 00:32:16.581
about the enigmatic figure named St Trina.

00:32:16.581 --> 00:32:17.581
---
Miquella of the Haligtree (glitch effect)

00:32:17.581 --> 00:32:22.640
St. Trina of the Cradlesong

00:32:22.640 --> 00:32:28.071
Perhaps the biggest in-game clue about St
Trina's true identity is Trina's Lily, which

00:32:28.071 --> 00:32:32.809
bears an undeniable resemblance to Miquella's
lily of unalloyed gold.

00:32:32.809 --> 00:32:40.059
Its description reads "A symbol of faith in
St Trina. Dulls the senses, preventing agitation".

00:32:40.059 --> 00:32:45.460
Naturally, it can be used to craft a bunch
of sleep-afflicting items, like St Trina's

00:32:45.460 --> 00:32:50.710
Arrow, which states that "The sweet oblivion
of sleep can become quite the habit", and

00:32:50.710 --> 00:32:56.200
tells of the priests of St. Trina, who "use
these arrows to spread their teachings". Though

00:32:56.200 --> 00:33:02.410
the Japanese description seems to specify
that these were more of a tool for their rituals.

00:33:02.410 --> 00:33:07.980
So it's largely left to your imagination as
to what rituals these priests might have been

00:33:07.980 --> 00:33:13.490
performing - though I will mention that..it
seems St Trina might actually be able to be

00:33:13.490 --> 00:33:20.010
found somewhere, within sleep. This is suggested
by Fevor's Cookbook, which reads "A record

00:33:20.010 --> 00:33:26.210
of crafting techniques left by a man who was
utterly captivated by St. Trina. He continued

00:33:26.210 --> 00:33:28.190
the search for her in his slumber."

00:33:28.190 --> 00:33:30.630
What's not left to your imagination, is St
Trina's appearance. While their child form

00:33:30.630 --> 00:33:35.529
seems to be engraved upon the hilt of St Trina's
sword , their feminine adult form is actually

00:33:35.529 --> 00:33:43.640
showed upon St Trina's torch, and even called
out by the torches description, which reads

00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:50.210
"The carvings depict St Trina, but in adult
form, somewhat unnervingly" . The carving

00:33:50.210 --> 00:33:56.840
is indeed unnerving, and it is certainly strange,
considering Miquella is supposed to be eternally

00:33:56.840 --> 00:34:02.580
a child. It raises the question - what has
to happen for Miquella to grow up into this?

00:34:02.580 --> 00:34:07.710
And why is this bizarre creature, the adult
form he takes?

00:34:07.710 --> 00:34:12.460
Another question worth asking I think, is
whether Miquella even has total control of

00:34:12.460 --> 00:34:18.109
St. Trina. What if he's in a similar situation
to Marika Radagon, where their alter-ego is

00:34:18.109 --> 00:34:23.409
an opposite, of sorts, and able to act almost
as if they have their own free will?

00:34:23.409 --> 00:34:28.510
Though while this is certainly a bit of a
disturbing view of what St Trina could be

00:34:28.510 --> 00:34:36.139
- we do have cut content that does reassure
me that their alter-ego is still a benevolent

00:34:36.139 --> 00:34:44.550
person. This cut content was first showcased
by Sekiro Dubi, and is TRULY ancient - existing

00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:49.619
in one of the oldest versions of the game
that we know about.

00:34:49.619 --> 00:34:55.560
Here, we can learn about St Trina's Crystal
Ball, which reads:

00:34:55.560 --> 00:35:00.720
"A crystal ball full of mist. Symbol of St
Trina of the Cradlesong.

00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:05.579
Copies dream mist from a sleeping being.
Dream mist was once used as an ingredient

00:35:05.579 --> 00:35:10.760
in rare and potent physicks.
May the quietude of slumber come to all and

00:35:10.760 --> 00:35:15.520
sundry, even to those whose red eyes burn
with the flames of frenzy."

00:35:15.520 --> 00:35:20.730
This reveals that this cut version of St Trina
once even had sympathy for those afflicted

00:35:20.730 --> 00:35:26.220
by the Flame of Frenzy. They even went so
far as to teach the merchants their songs.

00:35:26.220 --> 00:35:35.670
The cursed flame burns inside our eyelids.
Corroding the lines that separate us. That's

00:35:35.670 --> 00:35:41.410
what the instrument is for. The tambre of
its song calms the flame, however slightly.

00:35:41.410 --> 00:35:42.410
Caressing, gently, so that we don't blend
together. Our song derives from an old lullaby.

00:35:42.410 --> 00:35:43.410
Sung for us, long ago, deep inside our tomb.
But whoever it was sings no longer. Its melody

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:44.410
allowed us to sleep, despite the cursed flame.

00:35:44.410 --> 00:35:48.869
This description of Miquella's songs as a
lullaby is reflected by the modern-day Sleep

00:35:48.869 --> 00:35:54.760
Pot description, which reads "Like a lullaby,
or a quagmire, its light-purple haze irresistibly

00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:59.069
draws its victims down into sleep. Sweet dreams"

00:35:59.069 --> 00:36:04.130
This is the closest thing we have to dream
mist, which was an item you could once collect

00:36:04.130 --> 00:36:10.150
from sleeping enemies. After this, you were
supposed to sell it to the merchants, who

00:36:10.150 --> 00:36:12.859
used it to quell their flame of frenzy.

00:36:12.859 --> 00:36:19.270
But as the merchants once said - whoever it
was that sings, now sings no longer. And this

00:36:19.270 --> 00:36:24.589
is a detail that has remained intact even
in the final version of Elden Ring, with St

00:36:24.589 --> 00:36:30.220
Trina's sword stating that St Trina's "appearance
was as sudden as their disappearance".

00:36:30.220 --> 00:36:35.240
Something clearly happened to Miquella, that
prevented them from continuing their work

00:36:35.240 --> 00:36:40.260
as St Trina. And that is what we will discuss
next.

00:36:40.260 --> 00:36:44.280
---
Miquella's Promise

00:36:44.280 --> 00:36:50.810
At some point, Miquella embedded himself into
the Haligtree. Why he did this is never explicitly

00:36:50.810 --> 00:36:56.080
stated, so we kind of have to rely on the
environmental storytelling here instead.

00:36:56.080 --> 00:37:00.430
Now, Miquella famously watered the Haligtree
with his own blood since it was a sapling,

00:37:00.430 --> 00:37:07.290
so you could argue that he embedded himself
in it to simply feed the tree more - which

00:37:07.290 --> 00:37:20.960
I guess is possible, since the tree does eventually
wither without Miquella inside it. But I don't

00:37:20.960 --> 00:37:24.829
think that can be the only explanation for
why he embedded himself.

00:37:24.829 --> 00:37:30.109
For instance - look closely at the Haligtree
roots, and you'll see the form of a treelike

00:37:30.109 --> 00:37:36.250
woman. And where her womb should be, there's
a gap. A gap that once contained Miquella's

00:37:36.250 --> 00:37:43.069
cucoon, cradled by the Haligtree. Now, either
Miquella was attempting to fuse into and become

00:37:43.069 --> 00:37:48.290
this womanlike figure, who might even be the
adult form shown on St Trina's Torch...

00:37:48.290 --> 00:37:55.880
OR there was a rebirth occuring. This is a
cucoon..within a womb, after all.

00:37:55.880 --> 00:38:03.880
But whatever the intent here , it seems things
ended prematurely. For Miquella would eventually

00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:07.990
be ripped out of the womb, and the Haligtree
would split and decay.

00:38:07.990 --> 00:38:08.990
So. The Haligtree, now but a husk...I heard
speculation Miquella embedded himself in the

00:38:08.990 --> 00:38:09.990
Haligtree...but before he could finish, someone
cut the tree open and absconded with his infant

00:38:09.990 --> 00:38:10.990
form. Indeed, it seems those words held weight.
How vexing. That the All-knowing didn't have

00:38:10.990 --> 00:38:11.990
the full story...

00:38:11.990 --> 00:38:14.290
And so, when we arrive at the Haligtree, and
the town of Elphael that is built into the

00:38:14.290 --> 00:38:20.650
brace that supports it - the music hits extremely
hard. This place is just so sorrowful.

00:38:20.650 --> 00:38:29.849
For the Haligtree, and Miquella's Lillies,
are wilting - and all who live there are hoping

00:38:29.849 --> 00:38:32.359
- praying for their lord to return.

00:38:32.359 --> 00:38:38.109
I love the little detail of the guards looking
outwards, and sitting dejectedly. To make

00:38:38.109 --> 00:38:43.700
matters worse for them, it was here that they
realised that the sacred light inside them

00:38:43.700 --> 00:38:50.339
would explode upon their imminent deaths.
And yet in spite of this, their spirit ashes

00:38:50.339 --> 00:38:56.300
show their faith, and state "May the flash
of our deaths guide Miquella's return"

00:38:56.300 --> 00:39:01.780
And Malenia is here too. Holding to the husk
of Miquella. Dreaming. Waiting for Miquella

00:39:01.780 --> 00:39:06.500
to return, and believing full well that he
will.

00:39:06.500 --> 00:39:16.130
Corpse after corpse, left in my wake...
As I awaited... his return.

00:39:16.130 --> 00:39:20.930
Malenia's Set reveals that she believes her
brother will keep his promise..so what was

00:39:20.930 --> 00:39:29.160
that promise, I wonder? Was it merely to return,
or something more? How much does Malenia know?

00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:33.460
Why did she fight Radahn? We'll have to talk
about all that, and more, in another video.

00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:39.290
But not all here are hopeless. There's this
one phantom in the consecrated snowfields

00:39:39.290 --> 00:39:47.079
who has clearly puzzled out who took Miquella,
and is pointed towards the Omen himself.

00:39:47.079 --> 00:39:51.540
Give him back! Give Lord Miquella back! Mohg,
you rotten omen!

00:39:51.540 --> 00:39:57.410
Indeed, it was the demigod Mohg who somehow
broke into the Haligtree, and absconded with

00:39:57.410 --> 00:40:03.650
Miquella's infant form. And it's with him
this story ends. Or perhaps, it's where this

00:40:03.650 --> 00:40:07.200
story truly begins.

00:40:07.200 --> 00:40:11.690
---
Mohg's Promise

00:40:11.690 --> 00:40:17.900
So if you're not familiar, Mohg is the omen
son of Godfrey and Marika. Being an omen of

00:40:17.900 --> 00:40:23.750
royalty , he was born into a wretched mire
of filth in the subterranean shunning grounds

00:40:23.750 --> 00:40:30.329
below the capital - but unlike his brother
Morgott who reviled his accursed blood - Mohg

00:40:30.329 --> 00:40:32.260
revelled in it

00:40:32.260 --> 00:40:38.369
It was because of this accursed blood that
he chanced a meeting with an outer god, called

00:40:38.369 --> 00:40:43.829
the "Mother of Truth" . And as Mohg "stood
before her, deep underground, his accursed

00:40:43.829 --> 00:40:49.380
blood erupted with fire, and he was truly
besotted with the defilement that he was born

00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:50.619
into"

00:40:50.619 --> 00:40:56.099
Mohg is just one of many characters who discovers
a new identity in the ways that they have

00:40:56.099 --> 00:41:02.839
been discarded by the world. And how could
he not? For his defilement was validated by

00:41:02.839 --> 00:41:05.050
nothing less than an outer god.

00:41:05.050 --> 00:41:10.660
And as always, we know very little about this
outer god. We know she is called the "mother

00:41:10.660 --> 00:41:17.119
of truth", and the "formless mother". We know
that she "desires wounds", and "bestows power

00:41:17.119 --> 00:41:23.410
upon accursed blood". Her followers can thrust
their arms into her body to scatter bloodflame,

00:41:23.410 --> 00:41:34.020
and share in the Lord of Blood's power to
send bloodflies before them.

00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:44.339
But the one thing that all outer gods seem
to have in common, is that they require vessels

00:41:44.339 --> 00:41:50.610
to move through. So in this case, the Formless
Mother's vessel was Mohg. For example, the

00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:56.980
sacred spear he wields is a weapon, but also
an instrument of communion, and Mohg may well

00:41:56.980 --> 00:41:59.730
be doing her bidding with his actions

00:41:59.730 --> 00:42:05.619
These actions included him starting a new
dynasty, called Mohgwyn, deep below the earth,

00:42:05.619 --> 00:42:11.021
in the grounds of these ancient, dynastic
remains. This is a secret place. Difficult

00:42:11.021 --> 00:42:17.270
to reach - and it was here that Mohg brought
the infant Miquella, torn as he was from his

00:42:17.270 --> 00:42:22.809
cocoon. I mean, that's how we see him in the
opening cutscene - but in-game Miquella seems

00:42:22.809 --> 00:42:29.980
to be back within a new cocoon here. You can
even see it sat upon a giant pelvic bone,

00:42:29.980 --> 00:42:35.319
which seems to be a reference to the womb
of the Haligtree woman that he was literally

00:42:35.319 --> 00:42:36.920
ripped from [CREDIT: Quelaag].

00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:42.720
From the Remembrance of the Blood Lord, we
learn of Mohg's intent here. He wished to

00:42:42.720 --> 00:42:48.810
"raise Miquella to full godhood" and "become
his consort, taking the role of monarch".

00:42:48.810 --> 00:42:54.880
To this end, Mohg has begun soliciting blood
offerings to Miquella. That certainly explains

00:42:54.880 --> 00:43:01.160
the state of the many who reside here... According
to the Lord of Blood's exultation talisman,

00:43:01.160 --> 00:43:06.990
he proclaimed "Render up your offerings of
blood to your Lord. Drench my consort's chamber.

00:43:06.990 --> 00:43:12.800
Slake his cocoon's thirst. His awakening shall
herald the dawn of our dynasty"

00:43:12.800 --> 00:43:20.510
And then, to return to Mohg's Remembrance,
it's stated that "no matter how much of his

00:43:20.510 --> 00:43:26.559
bloody bedchamber Mohg tried to share, he
received no response from the young Empyrean".

00:43:26.559 --> 00:43:32.670
So maybe nothing will happen. Or maybe, according
to the Pureblood Knight's Medal "It is not

00:43:32.670 --> 00:43:39.119
yet time. For For Mohg yet slumbers beside
the Divinity. Be Patient. The new dynasty

00:43:39.119 --> 00:43:40.470
is nigh".

00:43:40.470 --> 00:43:44.800
What do you think? I mean, it's hard to know.
Even Gideon has no clue.

00:43:44.800 --> 00:43:45.800
Well I wonder what comes next...If he continues
his slumber within the cocoon, all would be

00:43:45.800 --> 00:43:46.800
well. But perhaps it would be safer to destroy
it. Miquella is the one thing that remains

00:43:46.800 --> 00:43:47.800
a mystery to me...

00:43:47.800 --> 00:43:51.200
But something does seem to be happening to
Miquella, in there. He has clearly grown,

00:43:51.200 --> 00:43:55.319
since being taken - so maybe his adult form
is manifesting...

00:43:55.319 --> 00:44:08.040
And personally, this all reminds me a lot
of Berserk. Spoiler warning - but there's

00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:13.150
this moment at the very end of the first chapter,
where Griffith betrays his companions in this

00:44:13.150 --> 00:44:19.480
sacrificial ceremony of carnage and bloodshed,
in order to be inaugurated and reborn as a

00:44:19.480 --> 00:44:21.290
god.

00:44:21.290 --> 00:44:27.140
This..really reminds me of that. It also reminds
me of a scene with Griffith where he allows

00:44:27.140 --> 00:44:32.520
himself to be abused, in order to get what
he wants.

00:44:32.520 --> 00:44:40.119
So..I wonder, what if this was also what Miquella
wanted? We know that he is extremely proficient

00:44:40.119 --> 00:44:47.070
at compelling others to love him, and Mohg
is clearly enraptured. We know that he is

00:44:47.070 --> 00:44:52.460
an empyrean prodigy, and we know that his
sister, who knows him best, has total faith

00:44:52.460 --> 00:44:55.470
that he will return.

00:44:55.470 --> 00:45:07.680
Or maybe maybe Miquella didn't predict this
at all, and is being completely taken advantage

00:45:07.680 --> 00:45:08.680
of.

00:45:08.680 --> 00:45:13.540
Or maybe he did intend to be taken, but is
going to get more than he bargained for with

00:45:13.540 --> 00:45:15.089
the Mother of Truth.

00:45:15.089 --> 00:45:22.680
Or maybe Miquella's fate is long gone. After
all, in a place called Miquella's Hideaway

00:45:22.680 --> 00:45:33.069
in Altus Plateau, we can loot the Amber Starlight,
which Seluvis mentions is the very fate of

00:45:33.069 --> 00:45:34.530
a demigod.

00:45:34.530 --> 00:45:45.329
Or maybe the cut content is very much removed
from the game because it doesn't fit the developers

00:45:45.329 --> 00:45:50.599
intent for Miquella. I hope you all bear in
mind that that is a possibility, as I would

00:45:50.599 --> 00:45:57.920
hate to promote ideas that are against the
developer's new vision for this character.

00:45:57.920 --> 00:46:01.990
But it's definitely a possibility, I think,
that we could one day enter the dream of this

00:46:01.990 --> 00:46:07.170
slumbering demigod. After all, once, there
was a cut character called Rhico, who was

00:46:07.170 --> 00:46:12.140
supposed to say the following, standing before
Miquella's cocoon at Mohgwyn Palace

00:46:12.140 --> 00:46:19.190
"Finally, I have found it..... St. Trina's,
no, Lord Miquella's cadaver... Such that I

00:46:19.190 --> 00:46:24.920
may aid you, O Lord... So please, I hope you
welcome your humble servant Rhico... Into

00:46:24.920 --> 00:46:30.040
your dream, the world of your heart......
Indeed, I beg you grant my wish, that when

00:46:30.040 --> 00:46:35.980
you transcend from empyrean to god, allow
me a place by your side....."

00:46:35.980 --> 00:46:41.480
Plus if we do get DLC, it's going to need
a new Great Rune to acquire, right? That's

00:46:41.480 --> 00:46:51.840
a big gameplay mechanic in Elden Ring. And
the only other ones that we know exist are

00:46:51.840 --> 00:46:57.990
Ranni's, which she cast aside, and Miquella's,
which presumably still resides with him

00:46:57.990 --> 00:47:03.650
So hopefully we get some DLC to answer these
questions. Or, more likely, DLC will give

00:47:03.650 --> 00:47:10.910
us more questions than we started with. That's
always how it seems to go. I bet they'll throw

00:47:10.910 --> 00:47:15.010
us some good curveballs, as they always do.

00:47:15.010 --> 00:47:19.190
But regardless, it's always a ton of fun to
specualte with you all. So if you're still

00:47:19.190 --> 00:47:49.760
listening - thank you for giving me your time
today..and subscribe for more! See you next

00:47:49.760 --> 00:47:50.760
time.

00:47:50.760 --> 00:47:56.760
---

